In this setting, inter-business sale of a computer to a manufacturing firm is a textbook producer product case. The wording matches the textbook relationship without adding extra conditions.

No qualifying word breaks the definition or scenario, so the answer is true.', 'FALSE — The claim is false. B2C classification of a printer depends on colourful retail branding rather than on the private household purchaser.

The section on what counts as a marketing product (goods and services, B2B and B2C) frequently contrasts two similar ideas side by side. A comparison statement is true only if the relationship is stated in the right direction and applies to the right concept pair.

